# Notes on the Stroke License

Stroke is a paid app, and all of its source is public. I want that openness
to be useful to people without making it easy to turn Stroke against its
users or its author. The license has two aims:

1. Keep out bad copies. That means apps built from Stroke that hide malware,
   or that pass themselves off as Stroke while sending license payments to
   someone else.
2. Keep everything else open. That means learning from the code, fixing bugs,
   contributing back, reusing parts of it in your own free or paid projects,
   and building a substantially new product on top of it.

The conditions only apply when you publish something. Using, changing,
building and running the code yourself is unrestricted.

Stroke is source-available, not open source. The Open Source Definition from
the Open Source Initiative does not allow conditions like the ones above, so
this is not an OSI-approved open source license.

Stroke has a free trial, and Stroke Pro is sold at https://stroke.click.
Buying it buys a license key for the Stroke app. It does not change these
terms, and you do not need one to use the source code.

